{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אתם", :translit "atem", :gloss "you (plural)"} {:he "אתם לכו קחו לכם תבן", :translit "atem lekhu kikhu lakhem taven", :gloss "you go gather yourselves straw"} {:he "אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים", :translit "atem re'item asher asiti le-mitzrayim", :gloss "you saw what I did to Egypt"} {:he "אתם נצבים", :translit "atem nitzavim", :gloss "you stand"} {:he "אתם עדי", :translit "atem edai", :gloss "you are my witnesses"} {:he "אתם נצבים היום", :translit "atem nitzavim ha-yom", :gloss "you stand today"} {:he "עדי", :translit "edai", :gloss "my witnesses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["אתם" "אתם לכו קחו לכם תבן" "אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים" "אתם נצבים" "אתם עדי"]}], :frame {:text "Israel's eternal standing is what qualifies them as witnesses. Isaiah 44:8 declares Israel witnesses ('אתם עדי'), and Deuteronomy 4:4 adjures them to be forever alive. Deuteronomy 29:9 ('אתם נצבים היום') establishes that Israel stands before God not temporarily but for all time, which is what enables their role as witnesses described in Isaiah 43:10 and 44:8.", :sources ["Isaiah 44:8" "Deuteronomy 4:4" "Deuteronomy 29:9" "Isaiah 43:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואביא אתכם אלי", :translit "va-avi etchem elai", :gloss "and I will bring you to Me"} {:he "תורה צוה לנו משה מורשה", :translit "torah tzivah lanu moshe morashah", :gloss "Moses commanded us Torah, an inheritance"} {:he "מורשה", :translit "morashah", :gloss "inheritance"} {:he "מאורשה", :translit "me'orasah", :gloss "betrothed"} {:he "ואפרוש כנפי עליך וגו'", :translit "va-efros knafai alayich v'gomer", :gloss "and I will spread My wing over you, etc."} {:he "ואבא בברית אתך", :translit "va-avo b'vrit itach", :gloss "and I will enter into a covenant with you"} {:he "וארשתיך לי", :translit "ve'erasatich li", :gloss "and I will betroth you to Me"} {:he "ואביא", :translit "va-avi", :gloss "and I will bring"} {:he "בביאה", :translit "b'vi'ah", :gloss "by bi'ah (entering)"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ואביא", :b "בביאה"} {:kind :other, :note "Read מורשה (inheritance) as מאורשה (betrothed) via al tikri."}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Kiddushin 2a establishes that a woman is acquired through money, document, or bi'ah. Hosea 2:21-22 uses betrothal language ('וארשתיך לי') for God's bond with Israel, and Hosea 3:2 also uses 'וארשתיך לי'. Ezekiel 16:8 ('ואפרוש כנפי עליך') and Ezekiel 16:8 ('ואבא בברית אתך') describe God's covenant with Israel in marital imagery. Deuteronomy 33:4 ('תורה צוה לנו משה מורשה') is read as 'me'orasah' (betrothed) rather than 'morashah' (inheritance), so that Torah functions as a betrothal document.", :sources ["Mishnah Kiddushin 2a" "Hosea 2:21-22" "Hosea 3:2" "Ezekiel 16:8" "Deuteronomy 33:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["אתם" "אתם לכו קחו לכם תבן" "אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים" "אתם נצבים" "אתם עדי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "אתם", :refs ["Genesis 1:17" "Genesis 1:22" "Genesis 1:27" "Genesis 1:28" "Genesis 5:2" "Genesis 7:13" "Genesis 11:8" "Genesis 11:31"], :n 500, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אתם לכו קחו לכם תבן", :refs ["Exodus 5:11"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים", :refs ["Exodus 19:4"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אתם נצבים", :refs ["Deuteronomy 29:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אתם עדי", :refs ["Isaiah 43:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "ואביא", :a-value 20, :b "בביאה", :b-value 20, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Read מורשה (inheritance) as מאורשה (betrothed) via al tikri.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:29.177120028Z", :model "glm-5.2"}